"<p>When Nitrobase runs behind a reverse proxy—such as its own Traefik v3 panel route, an external proxy, or Cloudflare—incoming TCP connections originate from the proxy rather than the end user.</p>\n<h2>Configuring <code>TRUST_PROXY</code> and <code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS</code></h2>\n<p>To ensure login rate limiting, API rate limits, audit logs, and security alerts (<code>security.new_login</code>) record the real client IP address:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">APP_URL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">https://panel.example.com</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">TRUST_PROXY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">1</span></span></code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>TRUST_PROXY</code> (default <code>false</code>):</strong> Only enable this when <strong>every</strong> request to Nitrobase arrives through a trusted reverse proxy (e.g. after setting <code>PANEL_BIND=127.0.0.1:3000</code>). If plain direct access is open, clients could spoof <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS</code> (default <code>1</code>, range <code>1–5</code>):</strong> The number of trusted proxies in front of Nitrobase that append to <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>. Nitrobase reads the IP that many entries from the <strong>right</strong> and ignores anything further left sent by the client.\n<ul>\n<li>Behind Nitrobase's own Traefik panel route only: <code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1</code>.</li>\n<li>Behind Cloudflare + Traefik: <code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=2</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong><code>APP_URL</code>:</strong> Set to your panel's public <code>https://</code> URL. Nitrobase marks session cookies <code>Secure</code> only when <code>APP_URL</code> starts with <code>https://</code>, and uses it for absolute links in invite URLs, notification messages, and the OpenAPI server URL.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Security Headers Middleware (Traefik)</h2>\n<p>Nitrobase manages a shared <code>secure-headers</code> middleware in <code>/etc/nitrobase/traefik/dynamic/middlewares.yml</code> for routed apps, including HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>TRAEFIK_HSTS_SECONDS</code> (default <code>31536000</code> — 1 year)</li>\n<li><code>TRAEFIK_HSTS_PRELOAD</code> (default <code>true</code>; set to <code>false</code> if any app domains might need plain HTTP in the future, since browser HSTS preload lists are difficult to undo)</li>\n</ul>"